Verdant_Key.Name = Verdant Key
Verdant_Key.Description = A key carved from living wood, threaded with roots that still reach toward something unseen. It hums faintly — as though the forest it came from has not yet let go.\n\nThose who carry it feel a pull toward the wild. Something ancient and patient waits on the other side.

Astral_Key.Name = Astral Key
Astral_Key.Description = Forged beneath a sky that no longer exists, this key shimmers with the light of stars too distant to name. Its surface is cold to the touch, yet drifts with the slow motion of constellations.\n\nWhoever holds it carries a fragment of the cosmos — and whatever was sealed within it.

Sunforge_Key.Name = Sunforge Key
Sunforge_Key.Description = Cast from metal at the heart of a dying star, the Sunforge Key radiates a warmth that never fades. Ancient smiths are said to have shaped it during a solar event that left no survivors.\n\nIt opens things that were never meant to stay closed.

Shadow_Key.Name = Shadow Key
Shadow_Key.Description = This key casts no reflection and leaves no shadow of its own. It was not made — it was drawn out of the dark by hands that understood silence.\n\nWhat it opens has never been clearly seen, only felt. A presence on the edge of sight that follows those who dare carry it.

Moontide_Key.Name = Moontide Key
Moontide_Key.Description = Pulled from the depths during a tide that comes only once in a generation, this key carries the weight of the deep sea and the pull of the moon above it. Its surface shifts like water that refuses to settle.\n\nIt is said to open locks that exist only between moments — thresholds visible only in the dark.

Rift_Key.Name = Rift Key
Rift_Key.Description = Found in a place where the world tears at the seams, this key does not belong to any lock that has been catalogued — yet every lock recognizes it.\n\nThose who study it report that it occasionally appears in two places at once. Neither instance quite solid. Neither quite gone.
